import { JsonReaderCopy } from "../model"

pub fn copy -> JsonReaderCopy = JsonReaderCopy {
  summary: "Use map to turn a checked JSON name into a greeting. It passes only a successful value to an ordinary function and preserves the original reason when checking fails.",
  taskTitle: "Build a greeting from a checked name",
  purpose: "Check that an API's name is a string, then make text such as Hello, Mio. If name is false, reject it without making a greeting. An empty string is valid text, so it produces Hello, with a trailing space.",
  typescriptBefore: "The TypeScript version treats JSON.parse's result as unknown, then checks for an object and a string name. Failure returns Name rejected; only a successful check calls the ordinary greet function. All three inputs are syntactically valid JSON.",
  benefit: "map combines nameDecoder and greet into greetingDecoder while keeping both original functions separate. Reuse the name checker elsewhere and add only the successful-value transformation here.",
  setup: "json is the alias for std/json. The annotation in let stringDecoder: json.Decoder<String> = decodeJson selects the string checker. json.field \"name\" stringDecoder creates nameDecoder for a required string name. Calls put spaces between the function and its arguments.",
  after: [
    "fn greet name: String -> String is an ordinary function. The colon gives its input type; -> gives its return type. It adds Hello, and a space before the name. Its input is the checked name, not JSON or a failure reason.",
    "json.map greet nameDecoder takes the successful-value transformation first and the checker second. The resulting greetingDecoder is still a function receiving Json, but its successful String is now the greeting rather than the original name.",
    "report uses match to distinguish parse's Left failure from Right value containing parsed Json. Right greeting from greetingDecoder value returns the finished text; Left _ returns Name rejected. The underscore ignores the detailed reason for this message.",
    "The output is Hello, Mio, then Hello, with a trailing space for the empty name, then Name rejected. main's do runs println calls in order, and _ <- discards earlier print results. Unit means there is no useful return value; effect and with Console fails ConsoleError declare console access and possible printing failure.",
  ],
  details: [
    "When nameDecoder fails, greet is not called and the same DecodeError is returned. map does not change failure reasons or accept a rejected value under a replacement name.",
    "The function passed to map has type A -> B. It creates B from a checked A, but cannot add a new DecodeError failure through that return type. Design an additional check separately if you need new validation, such as rejecting an empty name.",
    "map also does not turn a programming defect in the transformation into DecodeError. greet simply concatenates text here. Using map does not automatically make failures from arbitrary code into JSON validation errors.",
  ],
}
